  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef had three sequences of real numbers k1,k2,…,kNk_1, k_2, \\ldots, k_Nk1​,k2​,…,kN​, c1,c2,…,cNc_1, c_2, \\ldots, c_Nc1​,c2​,…,cN​ and x1,x2,…,xNx_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_Nx1​,x2​,…,xN​. Unfortunately, he lost the sequence xxx; the only thing he remembers about it is that\nx1⋅k1+x2⋅k2+…+xN⋅kN=0 .x_1 \\cdot k_1 + x_2 \\cdot k_2 + \\ldots + x_N \\cdot k_N = 0 \\,.x1​⋅k1​+x2​⋅k2​+…+xN​⋅kN​=0.\n\nChef's favourite expression is\nx1+c1+x2+c2+…+xN+cN .\\sqrt{x_1+c_1} + \\sqrt{x_2+c_2} + \\ldots + \\sqrt{x_N+c_N} \\,.x1​+c1​​+x2​+c2​​+…+xN​+cN​​.\nIts value is defined only if xi+ci≥0x_i+c_i \\ge 0xi​+ci​≥0 for each valid iii. Let's denote the maximum value of this expression  (over all sequences xxx such that it is defined) by FFF.\n\nHelp Chef find FFF and a sequence x1,x2,…,xNx_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_Nx1​,x2​,…,xN​ such that the value of Chef's expression is FFF, or determine that there is no solution (the value of Chef's expression is always undefined).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\le N \\le 10^52≤N≤105",
      "0&lt;ki≤2,0000 \\lt k_i \\le 2,0000&lt;ki​≤2,000 for each valid iii",
      "∣ci∣≤2,000|c_i| \\le 2,000∣ci​∣≤2,000 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (15 points):** N=2N = 2N=2",
      "**Subtask #2 (15 points):** ki=1k_i = 1ki​=1 and ci=0c_i = 0ci​=0 for each valid iii",
      "**Subtask #3 (15 points):** ki=1k_i = 1ki​=1 for each valid iii",
      "**Subtask #4 (15 points):** ci=0c_i = 0ci​=0 for each valid iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN real numbers k1,k2,…,kNk_1, k_2, \\ldots, k_Nk1​,k2​,…,kN​.\nThe third line contains NNN real numbers c1,c2,…,cNc_1, c_2, \\ldots, c_Nc1​,c2​,…,cN​.\nAll real numbers are given with exactly two digits after the decimal point.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, if there is no solution, print a single line containing one integer −1-1−1. Otherwise, print a single line containing N+1N+1N+1 space-separated real numbers F,x1,x2,…,xNF, x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_NF,x1​,x2​,…,xN​.\n\nIt can be proved that if a solution exists, then it is unique. Your answer will be considered correct if the absolute or relative error of each number on the output does not exceed 10−210^{−2}10−2.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n4\n1.00 2.00 3.00 4.00\n5.00 6.00 7.00 8.00\n3\n1.23 8.90 5.67\n-2.34 -9.01 -6.78\n3\n1.00 1.00 1.00\n1.23 8.90 -5.67\n2\n1.23 8.90\n-5.67 2.34\n2\n1.23 8.90\n5.67 -2.34",
        "output": "12.0761472885 28.6000000000 2.4000000000 -3.2666666667 -5.9000000000\n-1\n3.6578682316 0.2566666667 -7.4133333333 7.1566666667\n3.5802375027 15.5642936942 -2.1510203645\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The optimal solution is x=(28.6,2.4,−49/15,−5.9)x = (28.6, 2.4, -49/15, -5.9)x=(28.6,2.4,−49/15,−5.9). Then, x1⋅k1+x2⋅k2+x3⋅k3+x4⋅k4=28.6⋅1+2.4⋅2−49⋅3/15+(−5.9)⋅4=0x_1 \\cdot k_1 + x_2 \\cdot k_2 + x_3 \\cdot k_3 + x_4 \\cdot k_4 = 28.6 \\cdot 1 + 2.4 \\cdot 2 - 49 \\cdot 3 / 15 + (-5.9) \\cdot 4 = 0x1​⋅k1​+x2​⋅k2​+x3​⋅k3​+x4​⋅k4​=28.6⋅1+2.4⋅2−49⋅3/15+(−5.9)⋅4=0, and F=28.6+5+2.4+6+−49/15+7+−5.9+8≐12.076F = \\sqrt{28.6+5}+\\sqrt{2.4+6}+\\sqrt{-49/15+7}+\\sqrt{-5.9+8} \\doteq 12.076F=28.6+5​+2.4+6​+−49/15+7​+−5.9+8​≐12.076. This is the maximum value of Chef's expression.\nExample case 2: For each iii, cic_ici​ is negative, but xi+cix_i+c_ixi​+ci​ must be non-negative, so xix_ixi​ must be positive. However, all kik_iki​ are also positive, so x1k1+x2k2+…+xNkNx_1 k_1 + x_2 k_2 + \\ldots + x_N k_Nx1​k1​+x2​k2​+…+xN​kN​ cannot be 000. There is no solution."
      }
